<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Landtag of Prussia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1849">1849</a>–<a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Prussian Landtag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Landtag of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> was the parliament of the Kingdom of Prussia and later the Free State of Prussia. Under the constitution of 1850 it had an elected House of Representatives, chosen by a three-class franchise weighted by taxes paid, and an appointed House of Lords, which kept conservative landowners powerful until 1918. After 1918 it became a single democratic chamber, until the Nazis dissolved it in 1933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/landtag-of-prussia.jpg" alt="Landtag of Prussia" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berlin_Abgeordnetenhaus_1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
